Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 23 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 4, finding 11): THE CLOSURE MAP SAYS WHICH NODES
 NO EDGE JOINS, AND ITS BUILDER REFUSES A NEW ONE

A reader's supplement on the arcs main changed at Review 80 (agy-002's), its eleventh finding, not checked by
main. Two things: three nodes were added to the map with no edge (G:SE3, G:PF2, G:FK12), and debts of a later
day stood under a heading of an earlier one.

THE NODES. Counted here: 23 of the map's 192 nodes that are not debts are joined to nothing, the three among
them, and 79 of its 96 debts. Nothing on the map's page said so. NO EDGE IS ADDED: an edge is a statement of
what a node requires, answers or bears on, and that is main's. What is built:
  - the map's page ends in a section that lists the 23 and gives both counts;
  - the map's source holds the 23 by name, as found on 2026-11-12;
  - the builder refuses a node that no edge joins and the table does not name, and a name in the table that
    an edge has since joined or that is no node. The gate that builds the map runs it.

THE DEBTS. Main mended the list on 2026-11-12 (P-828). Read here on main's head: every debt under a heading
that names a day has a row of that day, but P-253, an older row which its heading says was made a debt on
the day it names. The builder now refuses a debt under a heading of another day than its row's, and holds
that one by name. A heading that names no day is not read. What was also seen, and is no fault by this rule:
three debts whose rows are of 2026-11-11 entered the list in a commit made eleven minutes after midnight.

The lock gains two tests. Planted: a name taken out of the table (the map as it stood when the three were
added); a name added that an edge joins; a name that is no node; a small register with two debts of a later
day under an earlier heading, with its twin; the held debt's name taken out. Each is reported, and the twin
is not.

The map is built again: its nodes and edges are unchanged, its page gains the section. The lock passes: 8
tests. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
